(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[8 1 "// Descriptors (PY5c; CPython's Objects/descrobject.c, funcobject.c's classmethod and staticmethod,"] [9 1 "// classobject.c's method, typeobject.c's super and slot wrappers): bound methods, functions as"] [10 1 "// descriptors, classmethod, staticmethod, property, __slots__' members, super, the slot wrappers"] [11 1 "// that show a built-in type's slots as methods, and the attributes of types, functions and methods."] [24 1 "// Method is a bound method: a function and the object it is bound to."] [31 1 "// ClassMethod and StaticMethod wrap a callable."] [33 12 "// made by classmethod(...), not a built-in type's"] [47 1 "// Property is property(fget, fset, fdel, doc)."] [51 27 "// a subclass of property"] [61 1 "// Member is a __slots__ entry's descriptor."] [70 1 "// Super is super(type, obj)."] [79 1 "// slotWrapper is a built-in type's slot as a method (wrapper_descriptor)."] [88 1 "// mappingProxy is a type's __dict__ read only."] [91 11 "// the type whose __dict__ it is, or nil"] [92 11 "// the mapping, when it is no dict (mappingproxy(UserDict()))"] [95 1 "// proxied is the mapping behind p."] [119 1 "// newWrappers are the built-in types' __new__ objects, one each."] [127 1 "// slotWrappers keep one wrapper per type and name, so that int.__repr__ is int.__repr__ (enum compares"] [128 1 "// a class's methods with its data type's and object's; PY5e, part 2b)."] [131 1 "// slotWrapperFor is built-in type m's slot for the special method name, or nil."] [158 2 "// the number protocol's binary methods (__add__, __radd__, __iadd__ ...): the Binary, RBinary and InPlace"] [159 2 "// slots, NotImplemented when they do not apply (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200: test_asyncio reads int.__add__)"] [184 6 "// wrap_ternaryfunc_r: the operands swapped, the modulus third"] [197 22 "// wrap_indexargfunc"] [208 4 "// object_str: tp_repr, never the type's own __str__ (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: a class with"] [209 4 "// __str__ = object.__str__, doctest's DocTestCase, recursed without end)"] [330 5 "// dict_subscript sees self's type: a subclass's d.__getitem__(k) calls its __missing__ as d[k] does"] [331 5 "// (queue 202: urllib.parse's _Quoter(safe).__getitem__ raised KeyError: test_http_cookies,"] [332 5 "// test_wsgiref's request_uri)"] [440 3 "// one object per type, so that object.__new__ is object.__new__ (enum's _find_new_ compares them;"] [441 3 "// PY5e, part 2b)"] [493 29 "// unicode__format__: an empty spec, a subclass's str()"] [527 1 "// hackCheck is hackcheck: m's __setattr__ called on self, whose built-in base nearest to its type overrides it"] [528 1 "// (object.__setattr__(str, ...) would jump over type's own)."] [538 22 "// of the built-in bases one can reach here, only type overrides tp_setattro"] [545 1 "// objectDir is object.__dir__: the instance's dictionary's keys and its class's attributes."] [592 3 "// object's wrappers are made on demand (slotWrapperFor), add_operators' names here"] [615 1 "// superArgs are super()'s zero arguments: the running function's first argument and its __class__ cell."] [653 2 "// supercheck: a proxy's __class__ (a class it pretends to be an instance of)"] [683 2 "// functions as descriptors, bound methods"] [690 2 "// types.MethodType(func, instance) (method_new)"] [716 2 "// method_descr_get: a bound method is not bound again (gh-113157)"] [755 2 "// slot wrappers"] [786 2 "// classmethod, staticmethod (funcobject.c): a subclass's instance is an Instance around the Go value, so every"] [787 2 "// slot unwraps; __init__ copies the wrapped callable's attributes (functools_wraps) into the dict"] [813 19 "// a classmethod made by a program, not a built-in type's descriptor"] [839 3 "// a built-in type's classmethod_descriptor: a builtin_function_or_method bound to the class (dict.fromkeys)"] [897 3 "// descriptor_get_wrapped_attribute and its setter: the dict first, the callable's value kept there"] [942 2 "// property"] [1074 2 "// __slots__' members"] [1155 2 "// super"] [1202 5 "// a built-in type's method, or a method descriptor in a heap type's dict (methodDescrs: _ast's AST,"] [1203 5 "// queue 202c: super().__init__ in a node class's subclass)"] [1231 53 "// a subclass of super: its type called"] [1253 2 "// mappingproxy"] [1255 2 "// mappingproxy(mapping), over a dict (PY6a: enum's __members__); other mappings are the data model's"] [1266 3 "// mappingproxy_check_mapping: PyMapping_Check, not a list or a tuple"] [1276 2 "// a built-in type's own slots' wrappers (ownSlots, registry.go) are in its __dict__ too (PY5e, part 2b)"] [1284 14 "// a built-in type's attribute descriptors (type.__dict__['__annotations__']: annotationlib)"] [1316 2 "// mappingproxy_richcompare: the mapping's own comparison (queue 202: mappingproxy({}) == {} was False; test_re's"] [1317 2 "// test_getattr compares a pattern's groupindex with a dict)"] [1342 2 "// mappingproxy_or: the mappings beneath, a proxy's unwrapped on either side"] [1465 21 "// inside the first mro()"] [1515 2 "// type_get_text_signature: the signature in tp_doc, for the types that have one here (func_new's clinic doc)"] [1526 33 "// type_mro: mro_implementation afresh, a metaclass's mro() builds on it"] [1560 3 "// recursive_issubclass's check_class"] [1585 1 "// checkSetSpecial is check_set_special_type_attr."] [1767 2 "// __module__ is func.go's (PY6d's R5: the function's module), which this init's order let override this one"] [1770 1 "// excSlots are the __slots__ values of exceptions (an exception class's instances are *Exception, not"] [1771 1 "// *Instance): PY6a, by the integration's owner, for test_exceptions' slotted exception classes."] [1774 1 "// setTypeBases is type.__bases__'s setter (typeobject.c's type_set_bases; PY6b's request: typing.NamedTuple"] [1775 1 "// assigns a class's bases): a heap type's bases replaced by types of the same instance layout, its MRO and its"] [1776 1 "// subclasses' computed again and their slots refilled."] [1795 3 "// a reentrant mro() has not set base's MRO yet: its __base__ is asked too"] [1821 2 "// nothing more when a reentrant assignment replaced the bases"] [1840 1 "// newStaticBase is tp_new_wrapper's staticbase (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's test_bad_new): t, or"] [1841 1 "// the first base along __base__ whose __new__ is not a Python class's own (slot_tp_new)."] [1849 1 "// newOrigin is the built-in type whose __new__ t's tp_new is (inherited along __base__ from the first one"] [1850 1 "// that defines it), CPython's tp_new pointer compared."] [1864 1 "// newAliases: the built-in types whose own __new__ here is CPython's inherited one (defaultdict's is dict_new)"] [1867 1 "// isNewWrapper: v is a built-in type's __new__ (tp_new_wrapper); a class whose __new__ is one keeps the"] [1868 1 "// __new__ it inherits (update_one_slot's special case), so that class C(list): __new__ = object.__new__"] [1869 1 "// makes lists"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[134 29] [152 37] [192 37] [196 34] [210 67] [221 63] [226 68] [231 67] [247 37] [264 37] [286 37] [293 38] [325 37] [329 25] [343 38] [348 37] [358 37] [381 37] [419 38] [424 37] [442 26] [456 29] [483 25] [485 38] [492 34] [506 37] [531 12] [531 22] [552 24] [554 24] [577 24] [595 31] [647 26] [658 24] [665 23] [708 34] [711 36] [721 54] [723 57] [746 55] [760 27] [798 26] [805 41] [812 40] [821 40] [840 27] [860 22] [880 27] [902 24] [973 38] [981 28] [983 56] [1023 42] [1049 50] [1059 53] [1064 48] [1065 26] [1076 26] [1083 31] [1084 32] [1093 22] [1099 26] [1103 31] [1130 26] [1137 26] [1143 26] [1149 26] [1158 43] [1197 51] [1204 29] [1210 36] [1241 29] [1247 29] [1260 38] [1263 30] [1282 23] [1283 36] [1299 25] [1311 31] [1344 32] [1384 47] [1400 51] [1413 39] [1421 48] [1424 23] [1436 34] [1442 45] [1457 25] [1476 43] [1486 47] [1500 26] [1510 25] [1565 28] [1618 22] [1622 46] [1624 25] [1628 49] [1630 27] [1647 29] [1664 29] [1692 29] [1705 30] [1742 23] [1753 30] [1761 28] [1779 4